difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "flat structure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a way of organizing a company with many  people sharing responsibility, reporting to one boss", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Boris mentioned that BFP Publishing follows a flat structure.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le06ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about the structure of a company.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hierarchical structure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a way of organizing a company with the responsibility following a vertical chain from top down", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Polygon followed a hierarchical structure. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le06ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "complex", "type": "name"}, {"content": "containing many different interconnected parts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A hierarchical structure is as complex as it gets. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le06ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to report to ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to work for (the person you report to is the person who evaluates you)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Employees work as one large team reporting to one boss. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le06ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "divisional", "type": "name"}, {"content": "separated into sections", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In a flat company you don't have as many divisional structures as in a hierarchical company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le06ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "functional", "type": "name"}, {"content": "organized according to role", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My job involves working with people with different functional expertise. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le06ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn10le06ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Making Comparisons: <span class=\"italic\">as \u2026 as </span>and <span class=\"italic\">not as \u2026 as  </span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to compare things, you don't have to use comparative adjectives. You can use two different structures instead. Varying your language in this way makes your writing and speaking more sophisticated.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you want to compare the qualities of two things that are equal, you use the structure <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">as  + adjective + as</span>.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Maria is <span class=\"strong\">as tall as</span> her sister.<br/> I am <span class=\"strong\">as qualified as</span> the boss.</span><br/><br/>  When you want to compare the qualities of two things that are not equal, you use the structure <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">not as + adjective + as</span>. <br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">France is <span class=\"strong\">not as sunny as</span> Bali.<br/> A flat company is <span class=\"strong\">not as bureaucratic as</span> a hierarchical one.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My responsibilities now are not as clearly defined as in my last job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A flat structure does not have as many levels as a hierarchical one. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Modals and Expressions to Ask for Clarification", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " In a workplace setting, when you are not sure what someone has said, you can use different expressions to ask for clarification. These are polite.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here are some expressions you can use to ask for clarification. <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What do you mean, ______?<br/> I'm not following you. <br/> Could you be more specific?<br/> So, are you saying ____?<br/> I don't quite see what you're getting at.<br/>  Could you give me an example? <br/> Does that mean _____?<br/> You lost me again. <br/> Could you explain what you mean by _____?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Could you elaborate a little more on that?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't quite see what you're getting at. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Could you give me an example? ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "With a partner, discuss different jobs you have had (salary, level of responsibility, stress, tasks, hours, etc.).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose two jobs. Discuss how they were the same or different.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 5 sentences describing how the jobs are similar or not similar. In your sentences, use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">as\u2026.as</span> and <span class=\"italic\">not as...as</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Decide which job was the better. Explain why. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences aloud.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I discuss different jobs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write sentences comparing jobs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read the sentences to a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "", "time": "2000", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: You never mentioned that you worked at Polygon. That's a big deal! How'd you like it there?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: It was interesting and definitely different from how they work around here.\n<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: What do you mean, interesting?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Well, Boris mentioned that BFP Publishing follows a flat structure. Polygon followed a hierarchical structure.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Uh? I'm not following you. Could you be more specific?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: For starters, a flat structure does not have as many levels as a hierarchical one.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: So, are you saying a hierarchical structure is like a\npyramid?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yeah. A hierarchical company is as complex as it gets."}, {"image": "", "time": "36500", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I see. Could you elaborate a little more on that?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Well, a flat company is not as bureaucratic as a hierarchical one. Employees work as one large team reporting to one boss.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I don't quite see what you're getting at. Could you give me an example?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: To say this differently, in a flat company you don't have as many divisional structures as in a hierarchical one. People might have several reporting lines.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I get it. Does that mean your job responsibilities are not the same as the last job?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Correct. My responsibilities now are not as clearly defined as in my last job."}, {"image": "", "time": "73500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Could you be more explicit?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: In other words, I have to be flexible and prepared to do a variety of different tasks, as opposed to doing only one task all the time.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I think I get it now.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: It's a cross-functional team ...<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Sorry, Kristi. You lost me again. Could you explain what you mean by cross-functional?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: To put it differently, my job involves working with people with different functional expertise. We are all working toward a common goal.<br><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: It does sound like a really exciting job!"}], "video_src": "engenn10le06ob03re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can compare different aspects of jobs in a conversation with a colleague. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can deal with communication breakdown.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about jobs and work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What are some things that make communication difficult at work?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What do you do when there is oral or written communication breakdown at work?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_tex